Z||000009||Black88GT||05-24-2001||01:32 AM||||OK here are *some* of the top of my head, I have a lot more.<P>1.  I heard it bolts right to the '88 cradle with the exception of one bolt.  True?<P>2.  What exactly do you need to buy from Chris West for the swap on an '88?  I am definitely getting him to do the wiring harness.<P>3.  I heard it bolts to the getrag so I am assuming this is true for the Isuzu?  Getrags are too damn expensive so I will just go with the Isuzu.<P>4.  Fiero axles or Lumina axles?<P>5.  Which cams should I use?  I want the wildest/best possible for an N/A engine.  I have no intention of forced induction.    <P>6.  Is the bottom end the same as a pushrod 3.4?  Like the crank, rods, pistons etc.?  I am asking so I know which parts I can buy.  I intend on having forged pistons and possibly crank if it isn't too expensive which it probably will be.  Probably use SBC connecting rods also.<P>7.  The dogbone on the back of the engine.  I saw one guy used a "fake" dogbone mounted to the firewall.  I would like to avoid this.  Anyway you can use that dogbone on the motor?<P>k I think thats it for now, thanks!||||reg||7
Z||000010||perks88gt||05-24-2001||02:21 PM||||Whats up black88gt, glad you found out about that 3.4 tdc we were talking about.  Couple things on what you mentioned:<BR>  Why the isuzu?  According to the 3.4TDC sites I have been on, the GETRAG is barely adequate.  GM had durability problems with the 3.4 TDC cars equipped with a manual trans.<BR>  I know the pistons are forged, dont know about the reast of the engine.<BR>  And yes, as cool as that guys emgine was, that rear engine strut atached to the fire-wall was pretty weak<BR>  I think that motor is the way to go with, specialy in high end HP mode, no trans-ripping torque.  later<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||05-24-2001||02:40 PM||||Yeah, did you get my email?  I sent you an email, but for some reason only certain emails to AOL accounts reach their destination.<P>I was thinking Isuzu for sheer cheapness.  I can't afford an 800 dollar Getrag every 6 months.  You can pick up generally low mile Isuzu's for 200 bucks.  Initially I might go with a Getrag, but have an Isuzu on standby with 3.83 gears from Bill's Isuzu.||||reg||7
Z||000012||THE BEAST||05-24-2001||02:45 PM||||Don't worry Black88GT the connecting rods on this engine are forge already!<P>I read that you could put Northstar pistons on it, which have higher compression.<BR>About 22 more hp.<P>You should try this out and, have fan keep us informed with wherever you find.(email me with any news)<BR> <A HREF="http://members.home.net/gtp/" TARGET=_blank>http://members.home.net/gtp/</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://angelfire.com/ca2/34Performance/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://angelfire.com/ca2/34Performance/index.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.ramairtech.com/cgi-bin/pg-product_live.cgi?Sec=1988-1995_W-Body&Pur=" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ramairtech.com/cgi-bin/pg-product_live.cgi?Sec=1988-1995_W-Body&Pur=</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000013||THE BEAST||05-24-2001||03:43 PM||||WOW I'm melting on this one NOOOOOOOOO WAAAAAYYYY this is it.<BR>I'm getting this engine and this mods but definably I will need this guy's phone # or email address or even he's mail address.<P>How about these match with 10.25 compression ratio pistons of a Northstar. Then to increase compression, the head is decked. Expect this to increase compression about a 1.0, which also will require the use of BETTER gas<P>That equals 11.25 comp/ratio which if you do the math it is a gain of about 35 extra ponies!<P>Hey 270 hp at the wheels this is for me a dream come through (this is like 340 hp at the fly wheel, no more Ferraris and,no forced induction)<P>I'm going to need some help here what would be needed to make this N/A 3.4 (9.25 comp/ratio) engine to run on 11.25 comp/ratio?<P>1. Would I need bigger injectors for instance or a bigger fuel pump?<P>2. And how about timing do I need to retard it or instead advance timing would be more desirable?<P>3. How about someone with a Dyno software?<P>4. Can anybody HELP ME?<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000014||msweldon||05-24-2001||05:37 PM||||his engine only produced approx. 240hp at the wheels and therefore 270hp at the crank.<P>there is still much to be gained with the cams and spark/fuel tables w/o having to go to higher cp pistons.<P>the 96' tdc has two knock sensors to allow running of different levels of octane.<P>msw||||reg||1
Z||000015||ray b||05-24-2001||05:49 PM||||11.25 is way up for street gas or do you plan on runing a mix in it?<BR>is the alum 3.5 olds v6 60 0r 90 deg motor? is that same as isusu truck motor rated at 240hp in 2001<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000016||88formula||05-24-2001||06:21 PM||||If the pistons for the DOHC engine are forged than why are the Silvolite replacement pistons cast and the Federal Mogul replacement pistons hypereutectic?<P>Maybe GM switched to forged pistons in 96. <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Will||05-24-2001||07:24 PM||||I read a '94 (I think) Lumina shop manual which stated that the pistons and crank are cast, but the rods are forged. I also think that turbo 3.1 Grand Prix had a forged crankshaft, which I think is dimensionally identical to the 3.4 crankshaft-&gt; (rare) source for forged cranks.<BR>Northstar pistons are hypereutectic.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Black88GT||05-24-2001||08:31 PM||||I was reading this one write up at one of the links posted on this thread.  Is it true that this motor has 4 cams?  I thought it only had 2 cams?  This is going to get expensive...||||reg||1
Z||000019||Sleeper||05-24-2001||10:21 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>I was reading this one write up at one of the links posted on this thread.  Is it true that this motor has 4 cams?  I thought it only had 2 cams?  This is going to get expensive...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>yep, TWIN DUAL CAM 3.4...2 cams over each head. rebuilds are $$$.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000020||terryk||05-24-2001||11:53 PM||||I know Mike Smith and before you run out and buy one, realize that with that cam setting and the changes (intake/headers), the engine is not street friendly AT ALL. <P>I've driven it with one particular cam timing and it ran nice, but bucked like a bronco until you got past 3000. From my last conversation with him, it pulls like all hell from from 3000 up, but it's not this nice easy to drive engine.||||reg||1
Z||000021||lowCG||05-25-2001||12:18 AM||||I'd had some thoughts of doing something like that to my motor,but it's already kind of"pipey" stock,however,I might try and cut down the runner length(1-2") from inside the plenum,and then polish the surface in there before welding it shut again.<BR>I made my own intake once using Stromberg slide valve-type carbs on an old car and it ran pretty much like Terry just described!<BR>I suppose nitrous would help any flat spots in the accelleration if there was a problem <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000022||terryk||05-25-2001||12:26 AM||||Yeah, nitrous does tend to "flatten" things out..... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000023||Pontiaddict||05-25-2001||02:16 AM||||Anybody notice, that in the third intake picture, that the runners coming out of the lower intake are blocking half the throttle body inlet? (well a qharter of it anyway) I'm sure it was an accidental coincidence but moving the throttle body out of the way would help it out. I'd also guess that that plenum is a little on the large side. The way the runners are so close together is causing some airflow disruptions.<BR>Not that i'm a professional or anything, but those would be areas that I'd work on<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||msweldon||05-25-2001||05:29 PM||||terryk,<P>Yes, I've thought about the bucking issues and low end drivability.  I don't plan on making any cam timing tweaks, just the intake, higher lift and longer duration cams and maybe modify the ecm fuel and spark tables.  It'll probably be smooth down low but have the lack of low-end grunt like an S2000 or NSX.<P>Mike made an adapter plate, that I'm purchasing from him, so I can run two left side manifolds and run a fiero-like exhaust.<P>btw, thanks for the eprom table, he's also buring me a prom with the setting you gave him.  <P>msw||||reg||1
