Z||000027||lowCG||05-26-2001||07:08 PM||||I think there's enough volume of open space around the throttle body,and the firing order of a six like that shouldn't allow any robbing of airflow from any one cylinder to the other;however,the runners themselves could be opened up(flared)towards the top to allow for a more greater volumetric charge that would help out the lower and middle ranges.<BR>Pretty tempting to go and do this to my TDC,but I'm in bodywork mode for the summer so it doesn't look like a $400 car anymore.||||reg||1
Z||000028||THE BEAST||05-31-2001||12:01 AM||||Hey, msweldon<P>"Mike made an adapter plate, that I'm purchasing from him, so I can run two left side manifolds and run a fiero-like exhaust".<BR>I don't get it, you mean a "Y" down pipe?<P>"btw, thanks for the eprom table, he's also buring me a prom with the setting you gave him."  <BR>Could you share with us what kind of eprom table is this one? And it's behavior specs(it's made to handle high RPMs or instead low RPMs) <P>In another words will this work with Micheal Smith custom's intake system or something like it?<BR>Because, if does I want one!<P>||||reg||5
Z||000029||Shaun41178||05-31-2001||01:49 AM||||i suggest you check out the latest issue of Pontiac enthusiast magazine.  Wllmaybe not the latest but it is the march april issue I think.  I believe it has a orange GTO on the front.  It tells how to get an extra 40 hp from the dohc just from bolt ons and without a custom intake.  It should still be on newsstands at barnes and nobles cause that is where I saw it yesterday.  It went from 173 hp at the wheels to 214 I beleive.  A big improvement<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000030||Toddster||06-01-2001||12:49 PM||||I was actually talking to Mike last night. I took his car for a test drive about 3 weeks ago. The engine is awkward looking and a tight fit in the Fiero Engine Bay. He had 99% of the bugs worked out, but it was years in the making.<P>The pros are:<BR>Incredible power and torque.<P>The cons are:<BR>A LOT of custom work is needed and the Getrag is not a good tranny for it. This is a HIGH rpm solution. Peak Torque is so high up the power curve as to make it a nightmare in traffic.<P>The engine has a "second wind". Accelerating thru 4500 rpm is very average, then around 5000 rpm you feel like you get punched in the back. <P>It's a great experiment and could make a lot of heads turn on the 1/4 mile track but if you want it for the street, forget it.||||reg||1
Z||000031||Will||06-01-2001||01:39 PM||||I've been wondering about building a plenum as he did around the entire stock intake system, moving the throttle body outside the plenum. Then you could cut holes in the sides of the runners and use solenoid operated flapper valves controlled by a fairly simple RPM sensitive controller to implement dual length runners. That might aid the lull in the 4500 RPM region.||||reg||1
Z||000032||lowCG||06-02-2001||01:57 AM||||Noticed that the August issue of the Pontiac enthusiast magazine is out,so I missed the article.<BR>Any idea what was covered in that April issue's artcle?||||reg||1
Z||000033||Shaun41178||06-02-2001||04:06 PM||||They Extrude Honed the upper intake manifold, put on a ported TB, underdrive pulleys, CAI, a catback exhaust, and a custom tuned prom chip.  Gain of 40 hp at the wheels||||reg||1
Z||000034||lowCG||06-03-2001||12:35 AM||||Wow!  That's a good improvement,wish the extrude hone process wasn't so costly,maybe I'll do it the hard way,with lots of abrasives.<BR>Thanks for the info.||||reg||1
Z||000035||THE BEAST||06-07-2001||05:37 PM||||Does anyone know where I can find some good aftermark cams for a 3.4 TDC?<P>"And here's why: (4/2001), I finally went back to the same chassis dyno shop in San Jose, the Mustang Ranch. I had .030" spring shims for the valve springs--allowing me to rev to about 7600 RPM before valve float".<P>What type of company makes these springs for Michael or he pursed it at a regular performance store or could he improve them from another engine? Because, I really want them.<P><BR>"Stock cams are set to about 8* retard for intake and 18* retard on exhaust. 10* of overlap.  The intakes felt best at this setting"<BR>And how he could get the cams to be so adjustable? Did he had someone made custom time gears or are these regular items that you can get for the 3.4 TDC at a regular performance store?<P>I know that you could get those for Hondas but could you actually improve these to work with the 3.4 cams? (In case availability wasn't existent).<P>||||reg||5
Z||000036||87GTZ34||06-08-2001||01:59 AM||||The stock timing 'cogs' on the TDC/DOHC are fully adjustable.||||reg||1
